      en: "The Museo de Ambiente Histórico Cubano, also known as Casa Diego Velázquez, in Santiago de Cuba, is one of the oldest surviving houses in the Americas. Built between 1516 and 1530 for Diego Velázquez, the first governor of Cuba, it combines Mudéjar and Renaissance architectural styles. The museum displays period furniture, ceramics, and paintings from the 16th to 19th centuries. Its thick stone walls and small windows reflect early colonial defensive needs. The building was restored in 1970 and is a National Monument. It offers a glimpse into the life of the Spanish elite in early colonial Cuba.",
